# Hard water and soap: scale is not soap scum
#
# The hard-water ions and carbonate scale are modeled. Dish soap is a declared
# surfactant material, but no fatty-acid soap species exists, so the bench cannot
# form the curd-like soap scum responsible for poor lather. That absence is the
# boundary this comparison exposes.
register lv2
add v1 water 100mL
add v1 CaCl2 0.002mol
add v1 MgSO4 0.001mol
add v1 dish_soap 2mL
look v1
inspect v1
new beaker
add v2 water 100mL
add v2 dish_soap 2mL
look v2
# A separate scale-forming control shows the calcium chemistry the engine does own.
new beaker
add v3 water 100mL
add v3 NaHCO3 1.7g
add v3 CaCl2 1.1g
look v3
